From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: avplumber patches <patches@local>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:35:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/transition_cuda: dip through a solid color

Add mode "dip" and a runtime "color" option (Y:Cb:Cr as 8-bit limited-range
codes, fractions allowed). Alpha 0..0.5 fades main to the color and
0.5..1 the color to overlay, so the color alone fills the frame at 0.5.
The host scales the codes to each frame's depth and range once per frame
and passes Cb/Cr per plane; both kernels take them and branch on the
uniform mode before any fade or wipe work. A dip sample reads only the
picture still visible (none at 0.5), so it costs at most what a fade does.
The overlay's alpha plane does not apply to a dip.
---
 libavfilter/vf_transition_cuda.c  | 90 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 libavfilter/vf_transition_cuda.cu | 36 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

